	affiliations = {Department of Materials and Life Sciences, Seikei University, Musashino, Tokyo, 180-8633, Japan},
	abstract = {Integrable quantum many-body systems are considered to equilibrate to generalized Gibbs ensembles (GGEs). A general mechanism of such relaxation to GGE has been shown for unitary evolutions of exactly solvable quadratic bosonic systems in the thermodynamic limit. Here, we explore the role of locality and interaction with surroundings in the relaxation by considering the reduced dynamics of a class of open systems weakly interacting with a reservoir, which is initially prepared in a locally perturbed GGE. The standard derivation of a quantum master equation fails to describe relaxation to GGE in the long-time limit in the presence of the initial perturbation. We investigate a proper quantum master equation that guarantees the relaxation to GGE to avoid this counterintuitive issue and describes the relaxation to the reduced state corresponding to GGE in the thermodynamic limit. In particular, we show that the stationary state of the open system is fully characterized by GGE of the reservoir, which is independent of the initial local perturbation. © 2020 Physical Society of Japan. All rights reserved.},
